Part 1 - My Understanding (Paraphrase Output)

In Part 1, I built a full end‑to‑end CRISP‑DM project using the heart disease dataset.
The goal was to predict whether a patient might have heart disease based on their medical features.

I explored the dataset, checked for missing values, and looked at correlations to understand which features 
mattered. Then I cleaned and prepared the data by encoding, scaling, and splitting it into training and testing
sets.

After that, I trained several models, like logistic regression and random forest, 
and compared their performance. I evaluated them using accuracy, confusion matrices, and 
ROC curves to see how well each model predicted heart disease.

Overall, Part 1 shows the complete data‑science pipeline—from understanding the problem to preparing the data,
training models, and evaluating results. All code and plots are included in my GitHub repository.
